WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — deterministic-null (45s) Narrator Hari

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.109
First, most AI benchmarks skip a zero-model control group that tests what simple lookup already solves.

2
00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.569
Second, on bounded math and database tasks,

3
00:00:10.569 --> 00:00:14.782
a frozen lookup table matched cloud AI on nine of ten tests.

4
00:00:15.222 --> 00:00:18.283
Third, on open coding tasks AI leaped ahead,

5
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:23.222
while caching verified answers cut repeat energy three point six times.

6
00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:27.386
Doctors never approve a new drug without testing it against a

7
00:00:27.386 --> 00:00:32.026
sugar pill. Yet AI leaderboards routinely pit one giant neural model against

8
00:00:32.026 --> 00:00:36.605
another without asking what a fast recipe book of verified examples solves.

9
00:00:37.045 --> 00:00:41.828
Testing a zero-model baseline first separates marketing hype from real reasoning,

10
00:00:41.828 --> 00:00:48.384
and saving verified answers turns expensive breakthroughs into cheap instant lookups the next time they appear.
